open-gym-log-frontend
Leptos (CSR) + Tailwind frontend for a private gym log API. Mobile-first,
follows the system light/dark setting.

Needs
  Rust 1.85+ (edition 2024) with the WASM target, and Trunk 0.21+
    rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
    cargo install trunk
  Trunk downloads Tailwind itself (version pinned in Trunk.toml).

Run
  trunk serve              (http://127.0.0.1:8080)

  The API must be running on 127.0.0.1:3000. Trunk proxies /api/* to it
  (/api/exercises -> /exercises), so the API needs no CORS. Change the
  address in Trunk.toml.

Build
  trunk build --release    (output in dist/)

Deploy
  trunk build --release, then serve dist/ with a web server that
    - forwards /api/* to the API with the /api prefix stripped, as Trunk.toml
      does in dev (/api/exercises -> /exercises), and
    - answers unknown paths with index.html, so client-side routes like
      /workouts/12 survive a reload.

Layout
  index.html         Trunk entry: Tailwind CSS + the Rust crate
  style/main.css     Tailwind import, where to scan for classes, the font
  fonts/             IBM Plex Mono woff2 files (fetch them: see fonts/README)
  src/main.rs        mount the app
  src/app.rs         routes and the bottom tab bar
  src/models.rs      the API's JSON types (keep in sync with the API)
  src/api.rs         one fn per API endpoint, named like the API's handlers
  src/ui.rs          shared class strings, small components, formatting
  src/pages/         one file per area: workouts (home too), workout_new,
                     templates, exercises

Pages
  /                        start a workout (empty or from a template), or
                           continue the unsaved one
  /workouts                calendar of the last 26 weeks, and history
  /workouts/new            log a workout; ?template=ID prefills its sets. Each
                           set shows the exercise's notes and the note of the
                           last set logged on it, and has its own notes. Until
                           it's saved or discarded, the workout is kept in the
                           browser's localStorage, so leaving the page or a
                           reload doesn't lose it
  /workouts/{id}           a logged workout, sets grouped by exercise
  /templates               list, with Start buttons
  /templates/new           create
  /templates/{id}          edit (replaces the whole template), start, delete
  /exercises               list and add
  /exercises/{id}          edit name and notes, delete, history by day
